/-! ## G. Public ByteArray `decodeCompactSize` — Core-divergence probes.
C1 `compactSizeDec` has NO canonicality / MAX_SIZE checks: where a
case says "Core ERRORS", Core `ReadCompactSize` throws but the C1 API
succeeds. These examples PIN the C1 behavior (VERIFIED in Lean) and
the Core verdict comes from the python reference (PROPOSED-side
evidence recorded in findings-w4/Y01.md, F-Y01-001). -/
-- non-canonical u16 form: C1 ACCEPTS, Core ERRORS (divergence)
example : decodeCompactSize (fromHex "fd0000") 0 = some (0, 3) := by decide
-- non-canonical u32 form: C1 ACCEPTS, Core ERRORS
example : decodeCompactSize (fromHex "feffff0000") 0 = some (65535, 5) := by decide
-- u64 form 0xffffffff: C1 ACCEPTS, Core ERRORS noncanon
example : decodeCompactSize (fromHex "ffffffffff00000000") 0 = some (4294967295, 9) := by decide
-- u64 form 2^32: C1 ACCEPTS, Core ERRORS toolarge
example : decodeCompactSize (fromHex "ff0000000001000000") 0 = some (4294967296, 9) := by decide
-- MAX_SIZE ok both
example : decodeCompactSize (fromHex "fe00000002") 0 = some (33554432, 5) := by decide
-- MAX_SIZE+1: C1 ACCEPTS, Core ERRORS toolarge
example : decodeCompactSize (fromHex "fe01000002") 0 = some (33554433, 5) := by decide
-- offset past end
example : decodeCompactSize (fromHex "01") 5 = none := by decide
-- truncated u16 form
example : decodeCompactSize (fromHex "fd01") 0 = none := by decide
-- empty
example : decodeCompactSize (fromHex "") 0 = none := by decide
-- offset decode mid-stream
example : decodeCompactSize (fromHex "00fc01fd0200") 2 = some (1, 1) := by decide
